eContinua_v2.py:31-35","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"FuenteContinua is a Tk window: its __init__ creates a Toplevel"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:68-74","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"Connection opens the selected VISA resource with pyvisa and queries *IDN?"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:36","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"The supply window names the instrument RIGOL DP832A"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:435-440","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"A channel is selected with :INST:NSEL and its voltage and current set points are written with :VOLT and :CURR"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:443-448","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"The voltage and current protections are written with :VOLT:PROT and :CURR:PROT on the selected channel"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:411-413","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"A channel output is enabled or disabled with :OUTP CHn,ON or :OUTP CHn,OFF"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:452-458","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"The measured voltage, current and power are read with :MEAS:VOLT?, :MEAS:CURR? and :MEAS:POWE? on a named channel"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:234-240","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"The channel labels state 30 V and 3 A for channels 1 and 2 and 5 V and 3 A for channel 3"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:216","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"The protection dialog states maximum protection values CH1 33V-3.3A, CH2 33V-3.3A and CH3 5.5V-3.3A"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:335-359","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"The protection entry defaults are 33 V and 3.3 A, and channel 3 starts at 5.5 V"},{"ref":"intefaz_FuenteContinua_v2.py:153-203","reviewed_by":null,"source":"upstream_code","text":"The transistor sweep writes 0 V and 0.4 A and then disables both channels"}]